cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its results, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "GreenCalculus Emission-Factor Accuracy Benchmark"
abstract: >
  A benchmark measuring how accurately large language models recall greenhouse-gas
  emission factors without tools, and — separately — how often they attribute a
  number to the wrong publisher. 467 questions across 45 sections and 75
  publishers, generated deterministically from sourced ground truth at data
  version 2026.187, phrased the way a practitioner asks rather than as canonical
  keys. Five frontier models were scored unaided; a paired 90-question run
  measures the effect of connecting a sourced factor lookup. Includes the scoring
  harness, unit reconciliation, every raw model reply, and a log of the six bugs
  found in the scorer itself.
authors:
